# TenderScope Backend — bc-tender-scraper

## Stack
- FastAPI on Railway, branch `master`, auto-deploys on push to origin/master
- PostgreSQL on Railway
- Local path: C:\Users\DAVIDSURF\Projects\bc-tender-scraper
- Test company: Pontem Group, company_id=8638

## Standing rules (never violate)
- NEVER run verification scripts or destructive operations against production DATABASE_URL — local DB only. Production data operations go through authenticated internal API endpoints (X-Internal-Key), never ad-hoc scripts.
- Historical records are NEVER deleted. Everything gets a lifecycle status instead.
- Do not commit until explicitly approved by the user. Always show diff + test output first.
- Every phase: implement → verify → review → approve → commit → deploy. One phase at a time, never implement future phases early.
- PowerShell environment: no `&&` chaining, commands run one at a time.
- tender_id string format is `{source}:{id}` (e.g. federal:42) in tender_outcomes — do not break compatibility.

## Architecture
- Lifecycle system: tenders have 17 lifecycle columns (P2-01), automatic transitions via pipeline/lifecycle_resolver.py (P2-02), closing_at parsed from deadline strings (P2-06), opportunity pipelines filter WHERE is_open=true by default with include_closed param (P2-07).
- include_closed=true semantics: skips BOTH the is_open column check AND deadline_is_open() — full archive access.
- Two scoring models coexist: construction_hybrid (opportunity_discovery.py, "AI Match Score") and business_pursuit (bd_recommendations.py, "Business Pursuit Score"). unified_opportunities.py merges them with dual provenance — NEVER blend scores into one number.
- tender_outcomes table (win/loss, per-company) is separate from lifecycle awarded status (global market state) — different concepts, do not conflate.
- n8n nightly jobs: lifecycle resolver 06:00, morning brief 07:00 America/Vancouver.

## Key docs (read when relevant)
- docs/audits/ — per-phase audit documents
- docs/VISION_HISTORICAL_INTELLIGENCE.md — why lifecycle exists (historical intelligence platform)

## Verification protocol for every change
- Run unit tests, show output
- LOCAL database only for DB verification
- Show before/after counts
- List every file touched
- Confirm which files were NOT touched (respect phase boundaries)
